<title>SPAIN: CYCLING-RESULTS IN THE FINAL STAGE OF THE RUTA DEL SOL.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-RESULTS IN THE FINAL STAGE OF THE RUTA DEL SOL.</headline>
<dateline>GRANADA 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results in the fifth and final</p>
<p>stage of the Ruta del Sol over 107 kilometres between Torrox</p>
<p>Costa and Granada on Thursday:</p>
<p>1.Johan Museeuw (Mapei) Belgium two hours 43 mins 20 secs</p>
<p>2.Erik Zabel (Telekom) Germany</p>
<p>3.Angel Edo (Kelme) Spain</p>
<p>4.Vjatceslav Ekimov (U.S. Postal) Russia</p>
<p>5.Jo Planckaert (Lotto) Belgium</p>
<p>6.David Etxebarria (ONCE) Spain</p>
<p>7.Angelo Canzonieri (Saeco) Italy</p>
<p>8.Georgo Hincapie (U.S. Postal) U.S.</p>
<p>9.Tyler Hamilton (U.S. Postal) U.S.</p>
<p> 10.Serguei Smetanine (Toscaf) Russia	all same time</p>
<p>Overall final standings:</p>
<p> 1.Zabel		     18 hours 30 minutes 33 seconds</p>
<p>2.Museeuw</p>
<p>3.Etxebarria</p>
<p>4.Canzonieri</p>
<p>5.Bingen Fernandez (Euskadi) Spain</p>
<p>6.Wilfred Peeters (Mapei) Belgium</p>
<p> 7.Miguel Angel Pena (Banesto) Spain    all same time</p>
<p> 8.Manuel Beltran (Banesto) Spain	 17 seconds behind</p>
<p> 9.Santos Gonzalez (Kelme) Spain		 41</p>
<p> 10.Ekimov					     47</p>
